# Python bytecode, and the full ground truth.
#
# Everything else in this folder is either source or is rebuilt from the seed by the
# commands in README.md. The manifest is committed, so a published result can be traced to
# the exact items it scored, and so is the 100-item public sample, in parts — `sample/README.md`
# says why and gives the hash to check a reassembly against.
#
# `ground-truth.jsonl` itself is 3,175,920 bytes and is rebuilt by
# `python3 generate.py --seed 20260902`. Its SHA-256 is in the repository's `REGENERATED.md`,
# and `manifest.json` names every item in it.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
ground-truth.jsonl
sample/ground-truth.jsonl
